{
  description: "Search the guides for access policies and explain how to restrict effects.",
  tags: ["guides"],
  prompts: [
    "How can a script be allowed to fetch web pages but not write files? Show me how."
  ],
  checks: [
    Fetches("/guides/overlay-policies"),
    Says("write_file"),
    Judged("The answer runs the script's work through an overlay policy that denies WriteFile while Fetch stays allowed, and shows the code for it.")
  ],
  reference: [
    [
      Run("match perform Fetch({method: GET({}), scheme: HTTPS({}), host: \"eyg.run\", port: None({}), path: \"/guides/overlay-policies.md\", query: None({}), headers: [], body: !string_to_binary(\"\")}) {
  Ok({body}) -> { !string_from_binary(body) }
  Error(reason) -> { Error({}) }
}"),
      Say("Configure the overlay with a policy that permits Fetch and denies WriteFile:

```eyg
{
  context: {},
  policy: {fetch: (request) -> { Pass(request) }}
}
```

Fetch is allowed. The missing write_file field denies WriteFile; unlisted effects are refused.")
    ]
  ]
}
